From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reverb256 <reverb256@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Jul 2026 00:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] feat: add SDR brightness control via NV_PLANE_DEGAMMA_MULTIPLIER

Add per-output SDR brightness support for HDR-capable displays on
NVIDIA GPUs. Uses the NV_PLANE_DEGAMMA_MULTIPLIER DRM plane property
(32.32 fixed-point) as a hardware-accelerated brightness multiplier.

This is the compositor-side half of the noctalia v5 SDR brightness
backend. noctalia calls `niri msg output <name> sdr-brightness <0..1>`
which lands here and writes the plane property. Only niri holds DRM
master, so the write MUST happen in niri (a standalone helper cannot
acquire master).

Changes:
- niri-config: Add sdr_brightness field to Output config
- niri-ipc: Add OutputAction::SdrBrightness variant
- tty.rs: Add NvBrightnessProps for detection/set/restore
- tty.rs: Apply sdr_brightness on config change / transient set

Usage:
  niri msg output hdmi-a-2 sdr-brightness 0.9
